    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Two years later, the answer arrives from the Middle East. In October nineteen seventy three, Egypt and Syria launch a surprise attack on Israel. When America rushes weapons to Israel, the Arab oil producers strike back with the most powerful weapon they have. They cut production and they embargo oil shipments to the United States. Within three months, the price of a barrel jumps from about three dollars to nearly twelve. Americans wait for hours in lines at gas stations. Pumps run dry. The government cuts the national speed limit to fifty five miles an hour, and even keeps the clocks on daylight saving time through the winter, just to save fuel. And Washington learns just how much power now sits on the other side of the world.",
